1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,172
It is two in the morning. The pipeline is red. The log has two thousand lines.

2
00:00:05,722 --> 00:00:06,713
Where do you look?

3
00:00:06,713 --> 00:00:08,531
Most people scroll to the bottom,

4
00:00:08,531 --> 00:00:09,798
and read the last line.

5
00:00:09,798 --> 00:00:11,119
That is the wrong place.

6
00:00:11,669 --> 00:00:14,528
Today you learn one habit: read the first error.

7
00:00:14,528 --> 00:00:17,506
Then we break a real pipeline four different ways,

8
00:00:17,506 --> 00:00:18,518
and fix each one,

9
00:00:18,518 --> 00:00:18,816
live.

10
00:00:19,366 --> 00:00:22,331
Name the hop. Test it alone. Change one thing.

11
00:00:23,881 --> 00:00:25,310
Here is what to expect.

12
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:30,660
One: the four places a SonarQube pipeline can fail, and what each one looks like.

13
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:35,562
Two: a method with five questions, that works for any failing pipeline.

14
00:00:36,112 --> 00:00:37,416
Three: a live demo.

15
00:00:37,416 --> 00:00:38,515
A wrong address.

16
00:00:38,515 --> 00:00:39,956
A server that is off.

17
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:41,741
A gate that never answers.

18
00:00:41,741 --> 00:00:43,388
And a gate that says no.

19
00:00:43,388 --> 00:00:44,486
We fix each one,

20
00:00:44,486 --> 00:00:47,163
and each fix shows us the next problem.

21
00:00:47,713 --> 00:00:49,889
Four: the common mistakes, and your turn.

22
00:00:50,439 --> 00:00:53,468
This is objective eight of the SonarQube domain.

23
00:00:55,018 --> 00:00:57,663
First, the four places a pipeline can fail.

24
00:00:58,213 --> 00:00:58,458
One.

25
00:00:58,458 --> 00:01:00,661
The scanner cannot reach the server.

26
00:01:00,661 --> 00:01:03,660
The message says: failed to query server version,

27
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:05,924
and it shows the address that failed.

28
00:01:05,924 --> 00:01:07,638
Either the address is wrong,

29
00:01:07,638 --> 00:01:08,923
or the server is off.

30
00:01:09,473 --> 00:01:09,730
Two.

31
00:01:09,730 --> 00:01:10,953
The server answers,

32
00:01:10,953 --> 00:01:11,725
but says no.

33
00:01:11,725 --> 00:01:13,591
The message says four oh one,

34
00:01:13,591 --> 00:01:14,684
or four oh three.

35
00:01:14,684 --> 00:01:15,842
That is the token,

36
00:01:15,842 --> 00:01:17,515
and we fixed it last time.

37
00:01:18,065 --> 00:01:18,444
Three.

38
00:01:18,444 --> 00:01:19,518
Everything works,

39
00:01:19,518 --> 00:01:21,096
but the gate stage waits,

40
00:01:21,096 --> 00:01:22,296
and then times out.

41
00:01:22,296 --> 00:01:23,875
There is no error at all.

42
00:01:23,875 --> 00:01:26,211
The reply never came back to Jenkins.

43
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:27,537
That is the web hook.

44
00:01:28,087 --> 00:01:28,425
Four.

45
00:01:28,425 --> 00:01:29,572
The gate answers,

46
00:01:29,572 --> 00:01:30,990
and the answer is no.

47
00:01:30,990 --> 00:01:33,352
The message says: pipeline aborted,

48
00:01:33,352 --> 00:01:34,769
quality gate failure.

49
00:01:34,769 --> 00:01:36,524
This is not a broken tool.

50
00:01:36,524 --> 00:01:37,739
This is your code,

51
00:01:37,739 --> 00:01:40,034
and the pipeline is doing its job.

52
00:01:40,584 --> 00:01:44,680
Four places, four different messages. The message tells you where to look.

53
00:01:46,230 --> 00:01:50,518
Now, the method. Five questions. Ask them in this order, every time.

54
00:01:51,068 --> 00:01:51,300
One.

55
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:52,401
Which stage is red?

56
00:01:52,401 --> 00:01:54,662
The stage view tells you in one second.

57
00:01:54,662 --> 00:01:56,401
Do not read anything else yet.

58
00:01:56,951 --> 00:01:57,196
Two.

59
00:01:57,196 --> 00:01:58,663
What is the first error?

60
00:01:58,663 --> 00:01:59,763
Not the last line.

61
00:01:59,763 --> 00:02:01,658
The first line that says error.

62
00:02:01,658 --> 00:02:04,226
Everything after it is usually just noise.

63
00:02:04,776 --> 00:02:05,160
Three.

64
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:06,184
Which hop is it?

65
00:02:06,184 --> 00:02:07,656
Jenkins to the scanner.

66
00:02:07,656 --> 00:02:09,320
The scanner to the server.

67
00:02:09,320 --> 00:02:10,792
The server to the gate.

68
00:02:10,792 --> 00:02:12,392
The gate back to Jenkins.

69
00:02:12,942 --> 00:02:13,289
Four.

70
00:02:13,289 --> 00:02:14,540
Test that one hop,

71
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:14,957
alone,

72
00:02:14,957 --> 00:02:16,069
outside Jenkins.

73
00:02:16,069 --> 00:02:17,320
One small command,

74
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:18,015
like curl,

75
00:02:18,015 --> 00:02:19,683
gives a clear yes or no.

76
00:02:20,233 --> 00:02:20,537
Five.

77
00:02:20,537 --> 00:02:21,571
Change one thing.

78
00:02:21,571 --> 00:02:22,180
Run again.

79
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:23,700
If you change two things,

80
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:25,951
you will never know which one worked.

81
00:02:32,001 --> 00:02:32,891
Let us do it.

82
00:02:32,891 --> 00:02:34,259
We start in Jenkins.

83
00:02:34,259 --> 00:02:35,012
We sign in,

84
00:02:35,012 --> 00:02:36,175
and open the job,

85
00:02:36,175 --> 00:02:37,475
cloud cart quality.

86
00:02:37,475 --> 00:02:41,376
It is the pipeline from the last lessons: build and test,

87
00:02:41,376 --> 00:02:41,718
scan,

88
00:02:41,718 --> 00:02:42,881
and quality gate.

89
00:02:46,931 --> 00:02:48,041
We click Build Now,

90
00:02:48,041 --> 00:02:49,267
and open the console.

91
00:02:49,267 --> 00:02:50,961
We have not touched the code.

92
00:02:50,961 --> 00:02:53,356
Someone just changed something around it,

93
00:02:53,356 --> 00:02:54,758
and we do not know what.

94
00:02:54,758 --> 00:02:55,400
Let us see.

95
00:02:55,950 --> 00:02:57,033
The first stage,

96
00:02:57,033 --> 00:02:58,048
build and test,

97
00:02:58,048 --> 00:02:59,671
does not need SonarQube.

98
00:02:59,671 --> 00:03:02,783
It compiles the code and runs the forty tests.

99
00:03:02,783 --> 00:03:03,460
It passes.

100
00:03:04,010 --> 00:03:05,624
Now the Scan stage starts.

101
00:03:05,624 --> 00:03:07,425
It tries to reach the server,

102
00:03:07,425 --> 00:03:08,667
and send the report.

103
00:03:08,667 --> 00:03:10,282
Let us wait a few seconds.

104
00:03:17,432 --> 00:03:17,699
Red.

105
00:03:17,699 --> 00:03:18,967
Failure number one.

106
00:03:18,967 --> 00:03:20,703
Question one: which stage?

107
00:03:20,703 --> 00:03:21,037
Scan.

108
00:03:21,037 --> 00:03:23,040
Question two: the first error.

109
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:24,843
We do not go to the bottom.

110
00:03:24,843 --> 00:03:27,714
We look for the first line that says error.

111
00:03:28,264 --> 00:03:28,978
Here it is.

112
00:03:28,978 --> 00:03:30,989
Failed to query server version.

113
00:03:30,989 --> 00:03:32,286
Call to the address,

114
00:03:32,286 --> 00:03:32,935
localhost,

115
00:03:32,935 --> 00:03:34,946
port nine thousand one hundred,

116
00:03:34,946 --> 00:03:35,400
failed.

117
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:37,282
The message does not say why.

118
00:03:37,282 --> 00:03:39,358
But it does give us the address.

119
00:03:39,908 --> 00:03:41,761
Notice what it does not say.

120
00:03:41,761 --> 00:03:43,813
A wrong token says four oh one,

121
00:03:43,813 --> 00:03:44,805
not authorized.

122
00:03:44,805 --> 00:03:45,136
Here,

123
00:03:45,136 --> 00:03:46,526
nobody even answered.

124
00:03:46,526 --> 00:03:46,725
So,

125
00:03:46,725 --> 00:03:49,504
two possible causes: the address is wrong,

126
00:03:49,504 --> 00:03:50,894
or the server is off.

127
00:03:51,444 --> 00:03:53,297
Question four: test the hop,

128
00:03:53,297 --> 00:03:53,694
alone.

129
00:03:53,694 --> 00:03:54,753
In the terminal.

130
00:03:54,753 --> 00:03:56,871
We ask the address from the log,

131
00:03:56,871 --> 00:03:58,923
port nine thousand one hundred,

132
00:03:58,923 --> 00:03:59,915
for its status.

133
00:03:59,915 --> 00:04:01,173
Nothing comes back.

134
00:04:01,173 --> 00:04:03,555
Curl says seven: connection refused.

135
00:04:03,555 --> 00:04:05,540
Now we ask port nine thousand.

136
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:06,996
It answers: status UP.

137
00:04:07,546 --> 00:04:12,965
So the server is healthy. The address in Jenkins is wrong. A typo, a very common one.

138
00:04:18,015 --> 00:04:19,601
The fix is in Jenkins.

139
00:04:19,601 --> 00:04:20,682
Manage Jenkins,

140
00:04:20,682 --> 00:04:21,187
System.

141
00:04:21,187 --> 00:04:24,070
We scroll down to the SonarQube servers.

142
00:04:24,070 --> 00:04:27,747
The server URL says port nine thousand one hundred.

143
00:04:27,747 --> 00:04:30,270
We change it to port nine thousand,

144
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:31,135
and we save.

145
00:04:34,685 --> 00:04:34,921
Now,

146
00:04:34,921 --> 00:04:35,923
a second failure.

147
00:04:35,923 --> 00:04:37,868
While we were fixing the address,

148
00:04:37,868 --> 00:04:41,228
a colleague stopped the SonarQube server for maintenance.

149
00:04:41,228 --> 00:04:42,171
In the terminal,

150
00:04:42,171 --> 00:04:43,645
that is the stop command.

151
00:04:49,195 --> 00:04:53,632
We run the build again. The address is right this time. Let us see what the log says.

152
00:04:54,182 --> 00:04:59,110
The build and test stage passes again. And the Scan stage is starting. Let us wait.

153
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:06,519
Red again.

154
00:05:06,519 --> 00:05:07,112
And look.

155
00:05:07,112 --> 00:05:10,734
It is the same message: failed to query server version.

156
00:05:10,734 --> 00:05:13,631
But the address now says port nine thousand,

157
00:05:13,631 --> 00:05:14,553
the right one.

158
00:05:14,553 --> 00:05:16,134
The symptom is the same.

159
00:05:16,134 --> 00:05:17,648
The cause is different.

160
00:05:17,648 --> 00:05:19,492
That is why we test the hop.

161
00:05:20,042 --> 00:05:22,202
We ask the server for its status.

162
00:05:22,202 --> 00:05:22,726
Nothing.

163
00:05:22,726 --> 00:05:23,773
Curl says seven.

164
00:05:23,773 --> 00:05:25,017
The server is down.

165
00:05:25,017 --> 00:05:26,064
Not the address.

166
00:05:26,064 --> 00:05:26,784
The server.

167
00:05:27,334 --> 00:05:28,637
We start it again.

168
00:05:28,637 --> 00:05:29,723
sonar.sh start.

169
00:05:29,723 --> 00:05:31,533
Then we watch the status,

170
00:05:31,533 --> 00:05:32,908
every five seconds,

171
00:05:32,908 --> 00:05:34,139
until it says UP.

172
00:05:34,689 --> 00:05:37,809
While we wait: SonarQube is three programs in one.

173
00:05:37,809 --> 00:05:39,619
A web server for the screens.

174
00:05:39,619 --> 00:05:41,429
A search engine for the data.

175
00:05:41,429 --> 00:05:42,739
And a compute engine,

176
00:05:42,739 --> 00:05:44,487
that processes your reports.

177
00:05:44,487 --> 00:05:46,296
They start one after another,

178
00:05:46,296 --> 00:05:48,044
and it takes about a minute.

179
00:05:48,594 --> 00:05:50,417
STARTING means: not ready yet.

180
00:05:50,417 --> 00:05:51,390
If you scan now,

181
00:05:51,390 --> 00:05:52,545
you can fail again.

182
00:05:52,545 --> 00:05:54,247
Always wait for the word UP.

183
00:05:54,797 --> 00:05:57,549
UP. The server is ready. We run the build again.

184
00:06:26,099 --> 00:06:27,319
We click Build Now,

185
00:06:27,319 --> 00:06:28,667
and open the console.

186
00:06:28,667 --> 00:06:30,079
Build and test passes.

187
00:06:30,079 --> 00:06:31,556
And now the Scan stage.

188
00:06:31,556 --> 00:06:33,032
Let us watch carefully.

189
00:06:33,582 --> 00:06:34,251
This time,

190
00:06:34,251 --> 00:06:35,253
the scan works.

191
00:06:35,253 --> 00:06:35,854
No error.

192
00:06:35,854 --> 00:06:37,124
The report is sent.

193
00:06:37,124 --> 00:06:39,463
The next stage is the quality gate.

194
00:06:39,463 --> 00:06:41,668
Jenkins now waits for the answer,

195
00:06:41,668 --> 00:06:43,673
and the timeout is one minute.

196
00:06:44,223 --> 00:06:46,076
Here is what this stage does.

197
00:06:46,076 --> 00:06:47,034
After the scan,

198
00:06:47,034 --> 00:06:50,357
SonarQube needs a little time to process the report,

199
00:06:50,357 --> 00:06:51,762
in the compute engine.

200
00:06:51,762 --> 00:06:53,615
Jenkins asks: is it finished?

201
00:06:53,615 --> 00:06:55,149
And what is the verdict?

202
00:06:55,149 --> 00:06:57,002
Then it waits for the answer.

203
00:06:57,552 --> 00:06:59,808
The answer should arrive by itself.

204
00:06:59,808 --> 00:07:02,258
SonarQube is supposed to call Jenkins,

205
00:07:02,258 --> 00:07:03,289
when it is done.

206
00:07:03,289 --> 00:07:06,448
Keep that in mind: someone has to make that call.

207
00:07:06,998 --> 00:07:08,395
While the clock runs,

208
00:07:08,395 --> 00:07:10,457
let us write down the evidence.

209
00:07:10,457 --> 00:07:11,988
Build and test: passed.

210
00:07:11,988 --> 00:07:12,853
Scan: passed,

211
00:07:12,853 --> 00:07:14,716
and the report was accepted.

212
00:07:14,716 --> 00:07:16,179
Quality gate: waiting.

213
00:07:16,179 --> 00:07:18,441
So the pipeline reaches SonarQube,

214
00:07:18,441 --> 00:07:20,504
and SonarQube takes the report.

215
00:07:20,504 --> 00:07:22,899
The problem is not on the way there.

216
00:07:22,899 --> 00:07:24,363
It is on the way back.

217
00:07:24,913 --> 00:07:27,678
Let us use this minute to look at the clock.

218
00:07:27,678 --> 00:07:28,683
In the pipeline,

219
00:07:28,683 --> 00:07:31,133
the one minute timeout is a safety net.

220
00:07:31,133 --> 00:07:31,825
Without it,

221
00:07:31,825 --> 00:07:36,160
a build that waits for an answer that never comes would wait forever,

222
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:37,542
and block the machine.

223
00:07:37,542 --> 00:07:40,307
A timeout turns silence into a clear result.

224
00:07:40,307 --> 00:07:41,187
Remember that.

225
00:07:41,187 --> 00:07:42,129
It saves hours.

226
00:07:42,679 --> 00:07:43,162
We wait.

227
00:07:43,162 --> 00:07:43,886
And we wait.

228
00:07:43,886 --> 00:07:44,851
Nothing happens.

229
00:07:44,851 --> 00:07:46,179
This is failure three,

230
00:07:46,179 --> 00:07:49,015
and the strange part is that there is no error.

231
00:08:05,565 --> 00:08:06,132
Time out.

232
00:08:06,132 --> 00:08:07,772
Timeout has been exceeded.

233
00:08:07,772 --> 00:08:10,483
The stage did not fail because of an error.

234
00:08:10,483 --> 00:08:12,626
It failed because nobody answered.

235
00:08:17,176 --> 00:08:18,878
Question three: which hop?

236
00:08:18,878 --> 00:08:21,496
The reply from the gate back to Jenkins.

237
00:08:21,496 --> 00:08:22,870
Let us ask SonarQube.

238
00:08:22,870 --> 00:08:24,179
We open the project,

239
00:08:24,179 --> 00:08:24,899
cloud cart.

240
00:08:25,449 --> 00:08:26,489
Look at the top.

241
00:08:26,489 --> 00:08:28,115
The quality gate: failed.

242
00:08:28,115 --> 00:08:30,586
SonarQube had the answer a minute ago.

243
00:08:30,586 --> 00:08:32,212
It never reached Jenkins.

244
00:08:34,262 --> 00:08:37,192
SonarQube reports back through a web hook.

245
00:08:37,192 --> 00:08:40,890
A web hook is a call that SonarQube makes to Jenkins,

246
00:08:40,890 --> 00:08:42,913
when an analysis is finished.

247
00:08:42,913 --> 00:08:44,518
We open Administration,

248
00:08:44,518 --> 00:08:45,495
Configuration,

249
00:08:45,495 --> 00:08:46,193
Web hooks.

250
00:08:46,193 --> 00:08:47,448
The list is empty.

251
00:08:47,448 --> 00:08:48,704
That is the cause.

252
00:08:52,254 --> 00:08:53,276
We create one.

253
00:08:53,276 --> 00:08:54,590
The name: jenkins.

254
00:08:54,590 --> 00:08:56,123
The URL: our Jenkins,

255
00:08:56,123 --> 00:08:56,561
slash,

256
00:08:56,561 --> 00:08:58,313
sonarqube dash web hook,

257
00:08:58,313 --> 00:08:58,751
slash.

258
00:08:58,751 --> 00:09:00,430
The last slash matters.

259
00:09:00,430 --> 00:09:01,598
We click Create.

260
00:09:06,648 --> 00:09:08,185
We run the build again.

261
00:09:08,185 --> 00:09:08,853
Build Now,

262
00:09:08,853 --> 00:09:09,922
and the console.

263
00:09:09,922 --> 00:09:11,660
The first two stages pass,

264
00:09:11,660 --> 00:09:12,328
as before.

265
00:09:12,328 --> 00:09:13,731
The scan is accepted.

266
00:09:14,281 --> 00:09:17,694
And this time, the gate answers quickly. And the answer is no.

267
00:09:42,444 --> 00:09:43,292
Failure four.

268
00:09:43,292 --> 00:09:44,401
Pipeline aborted,

269
00:09:44,401 --> 00:09:46,228
due to quality gate failure,

270
00:09:46,228 --> 00:09:46,619
ERROR.

271
00:09:46,619 --> 00:09:48,185
Look at what this means.

272
00:09:48,185 --> 00:09:49,946
The pipeline is not broken.

273
00:09:49,946 --> 00:09:50,990
Every hop works.

274
00:09:50,990 --> 00:09:52,686
SonarQube judged the code,

275
00:09:52,686 --> 00:09:55,100
and the verdict was: not good enough.

276
00:09:55,100 --> 00:09:57,252
The pipeline stopped the release.

277
00:09:57,252 --> 00:09:58,231
It did its job.

278
00:10:01,781 --> 00:10:03,363
Why was the verdict no?

279
00:10:03,363 --> 00:10:04,533
We ask SonarQube.

280
00:10:04,533 --> 00:10:05,702
The project page.

281
00:10:05,702 --> 00:10:06,184
Failed.

282
00:10:06,184 --> 00:10:07,216
And the reason,

283
00:10:07,216 --> 00:10:11,687
in one line: coverage on overall code is below sixty two percent.

284
00:10:11,687 --> 00:10:14,026
The gate wants at least sixty two.

285
00:10:14,576 --> 00:10:14,846
Now,

286
00:10:14,846 --> 00:10:17,209
the wrong fix is to lower the gate.

287
00:10:17,209 --> 00:10:19,031
The right fix is the tests.

288
00:10:19,031 --> 00:10:22,136
One class has no tests at all: Legacy Pricing.

289
00:10:22,136 --> 00:10:23,216
In the terminal,

290
00:10:23,216 --> 00:10:25,038
we look at the test folder.

291
00:10:25,038 --> 00:10:26,523
The file is not there.

292
00:10:28,573 --> 00:10:33,309
We add the missing test file, and commit it. One small commit, with a clear message.

293
00:10:38,359 --> 00:10:40,190
We run the build one more time.

294
00:10:40,190 --> 00:10:40,781
Build Now,

295
00:10:40,781 --> 00:10:41,726
and the console.

296
00:10:41,726 --> 00:10:43,261
We have changed one thing,

297
00:10:43,261 --> 00:10:45,506
so we will know exactly what fixed it.

298
00:10:46,056 --> 00:10:50,877
Build and test passes. The scan is accepted. The gate answers. And now, green.

299
00:11:16,227 --> 00:11:17,983
All three stages are green.

300
00:11:17,983 --> 00:11:19,024
The gate passed.

301
00:11:19,024 --> 00:11:21,171
We open the project in SonarQube,

302
00:11:21,171 --> 00:11:22,732
to see it for ourselves.

303
00:11:22,732 --> 00:11:23,188
Passed.

304
00:11:23,188 --> 00:11:25,464
And the coverage is above the line.

305
00:11:33,014 --> 00:11:34,631
Look back at what we did.

306
00:11:34,631 --> 00:11:35,536
Four failures.

307
00:11:35,536 --> 00:11:37,089
Four different messages.

308
00:11:37,089 --> 00:11:39,223
Four different fixes: an address,

309
00:11:39,223 --> 00:11:39,805
a server,

310
00:11:39,805 --> 00:11:40,516
a web hook,

311
00:11:40,516 --> 00:11:41,486
and some tests.

312
00:11:41,486 --> 00:11:42,586
We never guessed.

313
00:11:42,586 --> 00:11:45,366
We asked the same five questions each time.

314
00:11:46,916 --> 00:11:48,068
Five mistakes.

315
00:11:48,618 --> 00:11:50,666
One: reading only the last line.

316
00:11:50,666 --> 00:11:52,458
The first error is above it.

317
00:11:52,458 --> 00:11:55,082
The last line is usually only the result.

318
00:11:55,632 --> 00:11:57,473
Two: restarting everything.

319
00:11:57,473 --> 00:11:58,019
Jenkins,

320
00:11:58,019 --> 00:11:58,701
SonarQube,

321
00:11:58,701 --> 00:11:59,928
the server itself.

322
00:11:59,928 --> 00:12:01,224
It hides the cause,

323
00:12:01,224 --> 00:12:03,611
and sometimes it creates a new one.

324
00:12:04,161 --> 00:12:06,232
Three: changing two things at once.

325
00:12:06,232 --> 00:12:06,942
If it works,

326
00:12:06,942 --> 00:12:08,126
you do not know why.

327
00:12:08,126 --> 00:12:08,836
If it fails,

328
00:12:08,836 --> 00:12:10,966
you do not know which change did it.

329
00:12:11,516 --> 00:12:15,420
Four: scanning while the server still says STARTING. Always wait for UP.

330
00:12:15,970 --> 00:12:19,735
Five: lowering the quality gate to make the pipeline green.

331
00:12:19,735 --> 00:12:20,884
That is not a fix.

332
00:12:20,884 --> 00:12:22,479
It is hiding the problem.

333
00:12:22,479 --> 00:12:23,373
Add the tests.

334
00:12:24,923 --> 00:12:25,798
Your turn.

335
00:12:26,348 --> 00:12:30,252
One: change the SonarQube address in Jenkins to a wrong port,

336
00:12:30,252 --> 00:12:31,276
and run the job.

337
00:12:31,276 --> 00:12:32,620
Find the first error.

338
00:12:33,170 --> 00:12:34,519
Two: stop your server,

339
00:12:34,519 --> 00:12:35,501
and run the job.

340
00:12:35,501 --> 00:12:37,894
Compare the message with the first one.

341
00:12:37,894 --> 00:12:38,814
It is the same.

342
00:12:38,814 --> 00:12:41,084
Find the difference with a curl test.

343
00:12:41,634 --> 00:12:46,285
Three: delete the web hook, and watch the gate stage time out. Then create it again.

344
00:12:46,835 --> 00:12:51,486
Four: remove one test, and read the quality gate failure in the project page.

345
00:12:52,036 --> 00:12:54,788
Five: after each fix, change only one thing.

346
00:12:55,338 --> 00:12:57,066
Pause the video, and do it now.

347
00:13:12,616 --> 00:13:13,491
Quick check.

348
00:13:14,041 --> 00:13:16,025
What are the five questions of the method?

349
00:13:16,575 --> 00:13:21,375
Failed to query server version. Which two causes, and how do you tell them apart?

350
00:13:21,925 --> 00:13:25,082
The gate stage times out with no error. What is missing?

351
00:13:25,632 --> 00:13:28,896
The gate says failed. Do you fix the pipeline, or the code?

352
00:13:29,446 --> 00:13:31,706
Objective covered: M C eighteen,

353
00:13:31,706 --> 00:13:32,837
objective eight.

354
00:13:32,837 --> 00:13:34,037
Diagnose scanner,

355
00:13:34,037 --> 00:13:35,803
server and gate failures.

356
00:13:36,353 --> 00:13:38,423
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

357
00:13:48,973 --> 00:13:54,861
Next: the SonarQube mastery lesson. A real scenario, a check script, and a clean finish.

358
00:13:55,411 --> 00:13:58,739
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
